# DiFede Games Expert Context

**App:** Family game-night score tracker (Flask + PostgreSQL + SocketIO, port 5002).
**NOT:** A rules engine or digital board -- scores only.

## Must-Read Docs
- `APPLICATION_EXPERT_GUIDE.md` -- full architecture, all games, API, pitfalls
- `CREATINGANEWGAME.MD` -- step-by-step new game checklist + image creation
- `DEPLOY_ROCKY.md` -- live Docker deploy (`--scale web=2`)
- `README.md` -- service ops, backup, troubleshooting
- `.cursor/rules/theme-text-contrast.mdc` -- light-on-light text bug

## Core Model
- `games` = type definition | `active_games` = session | `game_scores` = all scores (save on every entry)
- `/api/scores` uses `active_games.id`; `/api/games/new` uses `games.id`
- `game_sessions_numbered` view provides `game_number` per game type (use in UI, not session IDs)

## New Game Checklist
1. INSERT `games` (+ `display_order`) + `game_details`
2. Generate image (see CREATINGANEWGAME image guide)
3. Template from `gin_rummy.html` / `sevens.html` + `DiFedeVariableRounds` + round partials + `PlayerPicker`
4. Route in `routes.py` + `SLUG_TO_URL`
5. Dashboard slug cases (card + table icons/Continue)
6. Jinja parse + `python tests/smoke_test.py`
7. Dev restart port 5002; live = push then Rocky pull + `docker compose up -d --build --scale web=2`

## Critical Pitfalls
- Jinja in JS: `function(){ {% if %}` NOT `function(){{% if`
- Light backgrounds MUST have `color: #212529` (dark themes use light body text)
- Kill stale processes: `lsof -i :5002` before Ubuntu restart
- Do not clone UNO Classic for plain Pattern A -- use Gin/Sevens + VariableRounds
- Live sync must create missing round rows (VariableRounds / applyRemote*)

## Current Games (id 1-11)
Five Crowns, UNO (group), UNO Classic, UNO Flip, Dutch Blitz, Trouble, Basic/Other, Kings Corner, Gin Rummy, Sevens, Skyjo

## UX Rules
Mobile-first. No emojis. Plain labels. Save immediately. Modals outside game container.
Round view + auto-rounds for most multi-round boards; Five Crowns stays fixed-round.
